# 08 Compiled-pattern serialization: pcre2_serialize_encode() and _decode()
# https://www.pcre.org/current/doc/html/pcre2serialize.html
#
# Not exposed by PHP.
#
# What it is: a compiled pattern can be turned into a byte string and
# reconstructed later in another process without recompiling. The closest
# thing PHP has is its internal per-process pattern cache. You cannot
# see that cache or warm it, and it is gone on restart.
#
# What it enables: precompiling a large pattern set at build or deploy
# time and shipping the bytes to workers. No compile cost at cold start.
#
# How the demo works: push compiles the pattern onto pcre2test's stack
# without matching. #save writes the stacked pattern to disk as bytes
# (this demo writes /tmp/pcre2-gap-08.bin). #load reads the bytes back
# onto the stack and #pop makes the DESERIALIZED pattern current. The
# subject then matches against it. Nothing on that path recompiles.

# Expect: 0: 2026
/\d{4}/push
#save /tmp/pcre2-gap-08.bin
#load /tmp/pcre2-gap-08.bin
#pop
    year 2026
